A keyword glued to its operand or to the next keyword: `:RETURN-1`,
`:IF(...)`, `:STEP-1` and `1:TO`. Records whether the formatter
separates them. `:TO` / `:STEP` after a closing paren or identifier
(`Len(aRows):STEP`) lex as member access, not as the keyword, so the
formatter must not touch them (the input reports that line as an error).
Suspected issue: #326 — no space is inserted between a keyword and a glued operand or before a glued `:TO` / `:STEP` (`1:TO 5`, `1:STEP-1` stay glued) even though the formatter recognizes them as keywords and recases them, and diag.step_spacing still warns on the formatted output (style guide step_spacing: "Put a space before `:STEP` in `:FOR` headers").
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Loops;
:PARAMETERS aRows;
:DECLARE i, j;
:FOR i:=1:TO Len(aRows):STEP 2;
:FOR j:=i :to 1:step-1;
:IF(j > 1);
aRows[j] := aRows[i];
:ENDIF;
:NEXT;
:NEXT;
:RETURN-1;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Loops;
	:PARAMETERS aRows;
	:DECLARE i, j;
	:FOR i := 1:TO Len(aRows):STEP 2;
		:FOR j := i :TO 1:STEP-1;
			:IF(j > 1);
				aRows[j] := aRows[i];
			:ENDIF;
		:NEXT;
	:NEXT;
	:RETURN-1;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:30-4:31 error unexpected_token: Unexpected number '2' in ':FOR' header - expected ':STEP' or ';' (missing space before ':STEP'?)
5:11-5:14 error keyword_uppercase: SSL keywords are case-sensitive and must be uppercase: use ':TO'
5:16-5:21 error keyword_uppercase: SSL keywords are case-sensitive and must be uppercase: use ':STEP'
5:16-5:21 warning step_spacing: ':STEP' should have a space before it: ':FOR i := 1 :TO 10 :STEP 2;'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:30-4:31 error unexpected_token: Unexpected number '2' in ':FOR' header - expected ':STEP' or ';' (missing space before ':STEP'?)
5:11-5:14 error keyword_uppercase: SSL keywords are case-sensitive and must be uppercase: use ':TO'
5:16-5:21 error keyword_uppercase: SSL keywords are case-sensitive and must be uppercase: use ':STEP'
5:16-5:21 warning step_spacing: ':STEP' should have a space before it: ':FOR i := 1 :TO 10 :STEP 2;'
